  "rationale": "The recording-specific posted agenda (retained-agenda), filed by the City Secretary, convenes the 'PLANNING AND ZONING COMMISSION WORK SESSION' of the Town of Addison on Tuesday, February 15, 2022 at 5:00 PM, with Call to Order and discussion of P&Z Regular Meeting items; the provider player (provider-player) shows the chair calling the Planning and Zoning Commission work session to order and its chapters (native-source-chapters) mirror the same agenda. The convening body is therefore the Addison Planning and Zoning Commission itself; a work session is a meeting format of that same body, not a separate institution. Ken Schmidt speaks as presenting staff (Director of Development Services for the Town of Addison), not a convener, and mentions of the City Council, the Sam's Club study, and the Unified Development Code project are topic/status references only — they do not make the Council or UDC Advisory Committee joint participants, and no joint meeting is proven. The feed addison-tx-planning-and-zoning-commission ('Planning and Zoning Commission meetings for Addison') directly matches this recording, since a commission work session is one of the body's meetings. Other supplied feeds cover distinct bodies or topic-only connections (Board of Zoning Adjustment is a separate numbered board; City Council, bond committees, TIF, Community Partnership, Comprehensive Plan Advisory, Public Briefings, Public Input, and UDC Advisory Committee do not convene here), so no additional feed membership is supported."
